			<div class="content" id="post-content-1193272">
									

<p>I've adressed the formatting errors, but that's really a minor issue.<br />
What concerns me more is that you said you haven't felt a &quot;hook&quot;, which means I might've failed to convery what I was going for.<br />
The hook I was trying to create, the source of the &quot;creepiness&quot; is the fact that throughout the entire article and experiment it is not made clear whether the &quot;entities&quot; perceived are illusions generated by the SCP or actual entities that are around us all the time, studying us, looking at us, and we just can't see them without the item.</p>
<p>Do you think a section about an agent\D-class walking along a facility\populated test environment and reporting seeing lots of entities everywhere watching people would help?</p>
<p>I initially feared such a section would be contrary to the secretive and secure nature of the testing, but it might be necessary</p>

